    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0583" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-14T18:00:00-04:00">June 14, 1938—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>152. Embassy’s 179, March 19, 1 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d781-f1"/> The
                    Department is of the opinion, in which Treasury concurs, that there is warrant
                    for accepting the Chinese Government’s interpretation with regard to interest
                    deductions and you are therefore authorized to inform the appropriate
                    authorities of the Chinese Government that the American Government accepts the
                    contention of the Chinese Government to the effect that interest for the second
                    half year on the amortization portion of Boxer Indemnity payments made during
                    the first half year may be deducted annually from the December instalment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
